# images/PINS — the base images every sandbox image is built from, pinned by
# digest (the sha256 of the image's contents), so a rebuild next month starts
# from the same bytes as today. Closes reference finding M2 (unpinned images).
#
# Format: one `NAME=registry/repo:tag@sha256:...` line per base image. The
# file is parsed with `read`, never sourced. A `# tag:` comment above each
# entry names the tag the digest is taken from.
#
# The digests cannot be looked up from the machine this was written on, so
# each value ships as UNPINNED. `./sandbox` refuses to build while any entry
# is UNPINNED, and so does each Containerfile. On a host with Podman, run
#
#     scripts/pin-images.sh
#
# once: it pulls each tag, reads the digest and rewrites these lines. Run it
# again when you want to move to a newer base; `git diff` then shows exactly
# what changed.

# The agent, credential sidecar and git relay images: Debian 12 with Node 22.
# tag: docker.io/library/node:22-bookworm-slim
NODE_BASE=docker.io/library/node:22-bookworm-slim@sha256:efd0ab5780c2d9ab1f0f869571a00d5edb17793bff4cce4a2792e3eb0ffc7562

